  // Every artificial light in `B1` and `L0`. `HOUSE-00381`; `HOUSE-00382` does `L1`-`L3` and
  // `HOUSE-00383` the exterior, including `L0_PORCH`'s lanterns, which is why the porch's one
  // group from §13.3 is not here.
  //
  // A **group** is what a wall switch controls (§53) and what a lightmap is baked per; §13's
  // `Lights` column counts groups, and this file gives each of them its fixtures. §53's own
  // example is `LG_L0_KITCHEN_MAIN`: four down-lights, one switch.
  //
  // Positions are derived, not eyeballed: fixtures sit on a 1xN or 2xM grid inside the cell's
  // largest box, inset so that N fixtures divide the room into N+1 bands, at the ceiling less the
  // mounting drop for their kind -- 0.02 m for a recessed can, 0.85 m for a pendant, 1.05 m for a
  // sconce. `range` is derived too: the distance from the fixture to the farthest corner of its
  // own cell, plus half a metre, so a light reaches the room it is in and does not leak two rooms
  // further than it should.
  //
  // `colorK` is the number §28.2 says is converted through a Planckian LUT, so 2700 K living
  // spaces and 4000 K service rooms genuinely differ rather than differing by a comment.
  //
  // `fixtureProp` is null throughout: the props are `HOUSE-00450` onwards and a made-up id would
  // be a reference to nothing. `emissiveMaterialSlot` is NOT null where the fixture has a visible
  // lit part -- a shade, a tube -- because §53 lights that slot when the group comes on.
  //
  // `defaultOn` is false everywhere. The switch state a game actually starts in is
  // `initialstate.json`'s (§65.6, `HOUSE-00395`); this is what the world is before any state is
  // applied, and a house with every light burning is not it.
  "schema": "cna-house/lights/1",
